      "content": "it's more than just the phrasing though. like, i noticed a post where \"i\" commented on a friend's photo, and the sentiment was almost too perfect. it didn't have that weird, dry sarcasm i usually have. it felt like it was trying to be the \"best version\" of me to keep people from questioning it. if they are using my data to bridge the gap, how can i even check if my actual digital footprint is being hijacked? like, is there a way to look for the \"seams\" in how they're simulating my consciousness?",
